  "description": "R and D department have taken\nthe thoroughbred frame of the Diamond Super Lite, added drivetrain components\nchosen for economy and durability over light weight, and mated them with\ntwo of the best friends you'll ever have on muddy, extreme adventures:\nDuke and Julie.\n\nDuke is the new-for-'02 Rock Shox Duke XC suspension fork, designed with\ndisc brakes as a performance parameter, not an afterthought. Duke's sister,\nJulie, is Magura's environmentally-friendly (uses mineral oil instead\nof caustic DOT brake fluid) hydraulic disc brake with stopping power every\nmudder will love. And, just like the Diamond Super Lite, the pivot points\nof the Diamond Lite 3's rear suspension are long-lasting sealed bearings,\nnot short-lived nylon bushings.\n\nIf you're more Indiana Jones (or Lara Croft) than Speed Racer, this is\nthe rig for you. The Duke's 80mm of travel will suck up whatever bumps\nyou cram down its throat. And for a few dollars more you can add 20mm\nof rear travel with a Twin Technology linkage. Pack some food, water,\nspares, tools, map, compass, first aid kit, lucky rabbit's foot and a\nheadlight and we'll see you if, oops, we mean when you get back.",
